MODIFICATIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This fork adapts Psi0's action expert to predict 64-d pre-FSQ SONIC motion latents for a
Unitree G1 cube-repose task simulated in `vibe`, rather than joint/hand actions. Per
Apache-2.0 section 4(b), the changes to the original work are:

ADDED (no upstream equivalent)

  scripts/data/vibe/                       Corpus pipeline: rollout collection in the vibe sim,
                                           frozen-SONIC-encoder latent extraction, LeRobot
                                           packing, and two diagnostic probes. See its README.
  scripts/train/psi0/finetune-vibe-repose-psi0.sh
                                           Fine-tune launch config for this task.
  NOTICE                                   This file.

MODIFIED

  src/psi/config/augmentation.py
      `ResizeImage` now interpolates with BILINEAR instead of NEAREST. On a task where the
      commanded colour IS the label, point-sampling a downscale drops thin or oblique coloured
      faces: a linear colour-visibility probe over Qwen3-VL image tokens scored yellow at
      AUC 0.908 under NEAREST and 0.965 under BILINEAR at the same 320x240 / 80 tokens.

  src/psi/config/transform.py
      `RealRepackTransform` and `SimpleRepackTransform` now emit `action_is_pad`, and
      `Psi0ModelTransform` forwards it. This is the TEMPORAL mask (chunk steps that ran past the
      end of an episode and were filled by clamping the index), distinct from `actions_mask`,
      which is a dimension mask. Upstream never consulted it. Used by evaluation only; the
      training loss is unchanged.

  src/psi/trainers/qwen3vl_mixin.py
      `PaddedCollatorForTogether` forwards `action_is_pad`. The collator copies an explicit
      allowlist of keys, so an unlisted key is dropped silently.

  src/psi/trainers/sonic.py
      1. The pretrained-action-header load now selects tensors by SHAPE compatibility rather
         than by a `transformer_blocks` name prefix. On the released
         `postpre.1by1.pad36.2601131206.ckpt.he30k` header this loads 497.5M of 497.7M params
         (99.93%, 174/181 tensors) instead of 479.2M, recovering `obs_proj.views_proj`,
         `obs_proj.enc_pos.pe`, `time_ins_embed.*` and `action_proj_out.adaLN_modulation` --
         none of which depend on the action space, since the expert's width is unchanged. Only
         7 tensors genuinely must be reinitialized. The change is a strict superset of the
         previous behaviour and cannot load a mismatched tensor by construction.
      2. `evaluate()` masks out padded chunk steps (previously hardcoded to ones with a FIXME),
         and reports three diagnostics: `vs_zoh` (error relative to a zero-order hold on the
         current latent), `drop_lang` and `drop_vision` (error penalty when the language or
         image input is permuted across the batch, destroying its correspondence while leaving
         its marginal distribution exactly unchanged). Enabled by default; set
         PSI_EVAL_ABLATIONS=0 to skip. Also suppresses the empty `hand_joints` metric bucket
         when action_dim <= 64.

Upstream: https://github.com/physical-superintelligence-lab/Psi0

